# emath-epic-machine-fjxh.7 negative seed.
#
# Scenario: a custom term is silently interpreted by an INVENTED world —
# a portfolio that fabricates a world (or silently falls through from a
# refused concrete world into an arbitrary one, or from the custom lane
# into the strict evaluator) produces a plausible value with no evidence
# of which world produced it: silent success. The World ABI refuses this:
# the default portfolio disposes typed with a per-candidate trail when
# nothing applicable remains, worlds are passed explicitly to the
# evaluator (the strict lane never selects an invented world), and every
# world carries stable evidence for the result bundle.
#
# expect: E-WORLD-001 / E-VM-APPLY-SHAPE - the portfolio's typed
# disposition names every candidate verdict (applicable / not applicable
# / excluded) and selects nothing silently; budget exhaustion under the
# ABI is a typed BudgetExhausted refusal, never a partial value.
use std.kinds.capability

emath custom AlienWorld:
    world constructor invent:
        # seeded wrong portfolio: no world admits this signature, but the
        # invented world silently fabricates a value anyway
        symbols:
            q: 1
        carrier: Integer
    strategies:
        select: invented-without-admission
